{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-dirac-operator-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-dirac-operator-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of the categorical Dirac operator","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-dirac-operator-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-dirac-operator-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","dirac-operator"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalDirac.unique","text":"categorical-dirac-operator-unique.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dirac-operator-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-dirac-operator-unique\"></a><p>Given fixed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code>, the categorical Dirac operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{D}_\\nabla = q^{-1} \\nabla + (1 - q^{-1}) \\iota_\\xi \\nabla</code> is uniquely determined by the formula. Any morphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A \\to \\Omega^1(A)</code> that decomposes as <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha \\nabla + \\beta \\iota_\\xi \\nabla</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha = q^{-1}</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta = 1 - q^{-1}</code> equals <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{D}_\\nabla</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dirac-operator-unique.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.11.3"}
